+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Lookup backend | Local embedded SQLite index built on each kiosk | On-site HTTPS directory; managed search service | Lookups complete from files on the kiosk with no service to run, as the HLD's offline tenets require. An HTTPS directory or managed search service would put runtime network access and service timeout or credential handling inside the registry. Accepts that each kiosk validates and rebuilds its own index per snapshot. |
+| Index build location | Index is built at import time, not lazily at first lookup | Build on first lookup after activation | Keeps the 250 ms lookup goal free of build cost and lets a failed build leave the previous snapshot active. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Deferred
+1. Index file location and retention of the superseded index after activation.
+2. Behavior of a lookup that overlaps activation of a replacement snapshot.
+3. Behavior at startup when the active index file is missing or fails an integrity check.
